                    <history>
                        <origin>
                            <origDate calendar="Gregorian" when="1356">A. D. 1356</origDate>
                            <note>Written by <persName role="scr">William Weston</persName>,
                                perpetual curate of Crich.</note>
                        </origin>
                        <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_832">Crich, Derbyshire.
                                Parish church</orgName>
                            <p>On fol. 1 (s. xv/xvi): <q>I <persName role="dnr" key="person_3960"
                                        >Richard Bankes</persName> vicar of Cryche geve and bequethe
                                    this boke to my parysshe C<supplied>h</supplied>urche of Crych
                                    per me Ricardum Bankes vicarium de Crich</q>. William de Weston,
                                vicar of 'Cruch', died in 1369. See Rowland Alwyn Wilson,
                                        <bibl><title>The First Register of Bishop Robert de Stretton
                                        1358-1385</title>, William Salt Archaeological Society, new
                                    series, vol. X, part ii (1907), pp.
                            83-84.</bibl></p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">At foot of fol. 1 (s. xvi): <q>Sub: de:
                                Re: Le: Te: J. N. <note type="editorial">[or H?]</note></q>. Compare
                                <ref target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_1845"
                                >London, Lambeth Palace Library, MS 145</ref>
                            <ref target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/org_165"
                                >(Crowland)</ref> for 5 other manuscripts with this
                            inscription.</provenance>
                    </history>
